The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 1 (reverse_1): reverse(nil) = nil.
Axiom 2 (opAnd_1): opAnd(false, X) = false.
Axiom 3 (opAppend_1): opAppend(nil, X) = X.
Axiom 4 (eqListNat_1): eqListNat(nil, nil) = true.
Axiom 5 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
Axiom 6 (reverse_2): reverse(cons(X, Y)) = opAppend(reverse(Y), cons(X, nil)).
Axiom 7 (opAppend_2): opAppend(cons(X, Y), Z) = cons(X, opAppend(Y, Z)).
Axiom 8 (eqListNat_4): eqListNat(cons(X, Y), cons(Z, W)) = opAnd(eqNat(X, Z), eqListNat(Y, W)).
Axiom 9 (prop_revApp_1): prop_revApp(X, Y) = eqListNat(reverse(opAppend(X, Y)), opAppend(reverse(X), reverse(Y))).

Lemma 10: reverse(cons(X, nil)) = cons(X, nil).
Proof:
  reverse(cons(X, nil))
= { by axiom 6 (reverse_2) }
  opAppend(reverse(nil), cons(X, nil))
= { by axiom 1 (reverse_1) }
  opAppend(nil, cons(X, nil))
= { by axiom 3 (opAppend_1) }
  cons(X, nil)

Lemma 11: opAppend(cons(X, nil), Y) = cons(X, Y).
Proof:
  opAppend(cons(X, nil), Y)
= { by axiom 7 (opAppend_2) }
  cons(X, opAppend(nil, Y))
= { by axiom 3 (opAppend_1) }
  cons(X, Y)

Goal 1 (prop_revApp): prop_revApp(X, Y) = false.
The goal is true when:
  X = cons(suc(X), nil)
  Y = cons(zero, nil)

Proof:
  prop_revApp(cons(suc(X), nil), cons(zero, nil))
= { by axiom 9 (prop_revApp_1) }
  eqListNat(reverse(opAppend(cons(suc(X), nil), cons(zero, nil))), opAppend(reverse(cons(suc(X), nil)), reverse(cons(zero, nil))))
= { by lemma 11 }
  eqListNat(reverse(cons(suc(X), cons(zero, nil))), opAppend(reverse(cons(suc(X), nil)), reverse(cons(zero, nil))))
= { by lemma 10 }
  eqListNat(reverse(cons(suc(X), cons(zero, nil))), opAppend(cons(suc(X), nil), reverse(cons(zero, nil))))
= { by lemma 11 }
  eqListNat(reverse(cons(suc(X), cons(zero, nil))), cons(suc(X), reverse(cons(zero, nil))))
= { by lemma 10 }
  eqListNat(reverse(cons(suc(X), cons(zero, nil))), cons(suc(X), cons(zero, nil)))
= { by axiom 6 (reverse_2) }
  eqListNat(opAppend(reverse(cons(zero, nil)), cons(suc(X), nil)), cons(suc(X), cons(zero, nil)))
= { by lemma 10 }
  eqListNat(opAppend(cons(zero, nil), cons(suc(X), nil)), cons(suc(X), cons(zero, nil)))
= { by lemma 11 }
  eqListNat(cons(zero, cons(suc(X), nil)), cons(suc(X), cons(zero, nil)))
= { by axiom 8 (eqListNat_4) }
  opAnd(eqNat(zero, suc(X)), eqListNat(cons(suc(X), nil), cons(zero, nil)))
= { by axiom 8 (eqListNat_4) }
  opAnd(eqNat(zero, suc(X)), opAnd(eqNat(suc(X), zero), eqListNat(nil, nil)))
= { by axiom 4 (eqListNat_1) }
  opAnd(eqNat(zero, suc(X)), opAnd(eqNat(suc(X), zero), true))
= { by axiom 5 (eqNat_2) }
  opAnd(false, opAnd(eqNat(suc(X), zero), true))
= { by axiom 2 (opAnd_1) }
  false

RESULT: Theorem (the conjecture is true).
